    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0343" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/4</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-01T22:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1914, 10 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Suggestion made to the British Government through you has not been communicated
                    to any other government but the President asked you to let us know if there is
                    the slightest intimation that such a suggestion might be effective
                        elsewhere.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d59-f1"/> He is anxious to do everything in
                    his power to avert war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d59-f1" n="1" xml:id="d59-f1-content">
                <p>See the Ambassador’s telegram No. 258, August 3, 6 p.m., <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>, <ref target="#pg37">p. 37</ref>.</p>
            </note>
